-- title:
--   Eq. (8.33) — the collective operator $S_z^{[n]}$
-- statement:
--   The collective operator $S_z^{[n]}$ on $n$ qubits is diagonal in the computational basis, with
--   $$
--   S_z^{[n]}|x_1\rangle\otimes\cdots\otimes|x_n\rangle=\frac12\Big(\sum_{l=1}^n(-1)^{x_l}\Big)|x_1\rangle\otimes\cdots\otimes|x_n\rangle=\tfrac12\,(n-2H(x))\,|x\rangle,
--   $$
--   where $H(x)$ is the Hamming weight (number of ones) of $x$. Weak collective decoherence is the decoherence whose operator-sum (or Lindblad) algebra is generated by $I$ and $S_z^{[n]}$; its decoherence-free subspaces are the eigenspaces of $S_z^{[n]}$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Basis states are functions $x:\{0,\dots,n-1\}\to\{0,1\}$.
-- source:
--   Bacon, Decoherence, Control, and Symmetry in Quantum Computers, arXiv:quant-ph/0305025v1, §8.5, eq. (8.33), p.114 (PDF p.131); Definition 8.4.1, p.114 (PDF p.131)

import Mathlib

namespace BaconThesis.WeakUniv

/-- **The collective operator `S_z^{[n]}` on `n` qubits.**
Bacon, *Decoherence, Control, and Symmetry in Quantum Computers*, arXiv:quant-ph/0305025v1,
§8.5, eq. (8.33), p.114 (PDF p.131): "S_z|i_1⟩ ⊗ |i_2⟩ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ |i_n⟩ = ½ (Σ_{l=1}^n (−1)^{i_l})
|i_1⟩ ⊗ |i_2⟩ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ |i_n⟩", and §9.1.1, p.125 (PDF p.142): weak collective decoherence has OSR
algebra generated by `{I, S_z^{[n]}}` (Definition 8.4.1, p.114).

`Sz n` is the diagonal matrix with entry `½ Σ_l (−1)^{x_l}` at the basis state `|x⟩`,
i.e. `½ (n − 2 H(x))` with `H(x)` the Hamming weight (8.34).

**Formalization Note.** Basis states are `x : Fin n → Fin 2`, qubits `0, …, n−1`. -/
noncomputable def Sz (n : ℕ) : Matrix (Fin n → Fin 2) (Fin n → Fin 2) ℂ :=
  Matrix.diagonal fun x => (1 / 2 : ℂ) * ∑ l, (-1 : ℂ) ^ (x l : ℕ)

end BaconThesis.WeakUniv


